    "type": "html",
    "content": "<div class=\"book-content\">\n    <h3>🌟 What is Jiva?</h3>\n    <p><strong>Jiva</strong> (soul) is a living, conscious entity possessing infinite knowledge, infinite perception, infinite bliss, and infinite power in its pure state. Unlike lifeless matter (Ajiva), Jiva has consciousness (Chetana) and the ability to experience happiness and sorrow.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"concept-card\">\n        <h3>Characteristics of Jiva</h3>\n        <ul class=\"vows-list\">\n            <li><strong>Consciousness (Chetana):</strong> The defining characteristic that separates soul from matter.</li>\n            <li><strong>Formless (Amurta):</strong> Soul has no physical form, color, or smell.</li>\n            <li><strong>Equal to Body Size:</strong> The soul expands or contracts to fill the body it inhabits (like lamplight in a room).</li>\n            <li><strong>Eternal (Nitya):</strong> Soul is never created nor destroyed - only transforms.</li>\n            <li><strong>Infinite Capabilities:</strong> Each soul possesses infinite knowledge (Anant Jnana), infinite perception (Anant Darshan), infinite bliss (Anant Sukha), and infinite power (Anant Virya) when liberated.</li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"concept-card\">\n        <h3>Classification of Jivas</h3>\n        <p><strong>Based on Senses:</strong></p>\n        <ul class=\"vows-list\">\n            <li><strong>Ekendriya:</strong> One-sensed (touch only) - Plants, microorganisms</li>\n            <li><strong>Dvindriya:</strong> Two-sensed (touch + taste) - Worms, leeches</li>\n            <li><strong>Trindriya:</strong> Three-sensed (+ smell) - Ants, lice</li>\n            <li><strong>Chaturindriya:</strong> Four-sensed (+ sight) - Bees, mosquitoes</li>\n            <li><strong>Panchendriya:</strong> Five-sensed (+ hearing) - Animals, birds, humans, gods, hell-beings</li>\n        </ul>\n        <p style=\"margin-top: 1rem;\"><strong>Based on Liberation State:</strong></p>\n        <ul class=\"vows-list\">\n            <li><strong>Samsari Jiva:</strong> Souls wandering in the cycle of birth and death</li>\n            <li><strong>Mukta Jiva (Siddha):</strong> Liberated souls who have destroyed all karmas</li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"quote-box\">\n        \"The soul is your true self. Realizing this is the first step toward liberation.\"\n    </div>\n</div>"
