    "subtitle": "The Second Tattva - Lifeless Entities",
    "type": "html",
    "content": "<div class=\"book-content\">\n    <h3>💎 What is Ajiva?</h3>\n    <p><strong>Ajiva</strong> refers to all lifeless entities that lack consciousness. While Jiva is the only conscious entity, Ajiva comprises everything else in the universe. Ajiva does not experience pleasure or pain and cannot attain liberation.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"concept-card\">\n        <h3>Five Types of Ajiva (Pancha Dravya)</h3>\n        <ul class=\"vows-list\">\n            <li><strong>1. Pudgala (Matter):</strong> Has form, color, taste, smell, and touch. Includes all physical objects, karma particles, and our bodies. Can be perceived by senses.</li>\n            <li><strong>2. Dharma Dravya (Medium of Motion):</strong> Invisible substance that enables souls and matter to move. Like water helps fish swim, Dharma helps movement. Not \"religion\" but a physical medium.</li>\n            <li><strong>3. Adharma Dravya (Medium of Rest):</strong> Invisible substance that enables souls and matter to rest/stop. Like shade providing rest to travelers.</li>\n            <li><strong>4. Akasha (Space):</strong> Provides room for all substances to exist. Infinite and formless. Without space, nothing could exist.</li>\n            <li><strong>5. Kala (Time):</strong> Enables change, transformation, and  movement. Helps measure duration and sequence of events.</li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"concept-card\">\n        <h3>Key Differences: Jiva vs Ajiva</h3>\n        <table style=\"width: 100%; margin-top: 1rem;\">\n            <tr>\n                <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.5rem;\">Jiva</th>\n                <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.5rem;\">Ajiva</th>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Conscious (Chetana)</td>\n                <td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Unconscious (Acetana)</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Can attain liberation</td>\n                <td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Cannot attain liberation</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Experiences karma</td>\n                <td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Does not experience karma</td>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n                <td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Formless (Amurta)</td>\n                <td style=\"padding: 0.5rem;\">Matter has form, others formless</td>\n            </tr>\n        </table>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"quote-box\">\n        \"Understanding that the body, wealth, and worldly objects are Ajiva (non-self) helps develop detachment.\"\n    </div>\n</div>"
